// Stable quick sort family, query owned by stable_quick_sort_lib. Every stable
// partition but the sliding and the block ones, so the rotation, encoded and
// masked partitions, the masked one by each of its two walks, by every rotation,
// 60 entries. The sliding partition gathers the matches in one block riding
// behind the scan, `O(n + m r)` moves for `m` matches in `r` runs, which on a
// split of random keys is about `n^2 / 16`: a minute at 2^18 elements, so it is
// measured by the record and not catalogued. The block partition works through a
// workspace its caller lends, which the quick sort has none of, and is the
// rotation partition without one.

StableQuickSorts: SortingAlgorithm = SortingAlgorithm<StableQuickSort<
    part = _ - { SlidingPartition, BlockPartition },
    rot = _
>>
